# Tesserafin Server @VERSION@ — portable Linux archive (@RID@)

This archive is the *portable* distribution: the same application and web payload
as the `.deb` and `.rpm` packages, unpacked wherever you want it.

**It installs nothing.** It creates no user, registers no systemd service and
writes nothing outside the directories you give it on the command line. If you
want a managed service, install the `.deb` or the `.rpm` instead.

## Layout

```
bin/tesserafin                  symlink into lib/tesserafin/tesserafin
lib/tesserafin/                 the server application (self-contained .NET build)
lib/tesserafin/ffmpeg/ffmpeg    the bundled, checksum-pinned media encoder
lib/tesserafin/ffmpeg/ffprobe
share/tesserafin/web/           the bundled Tesserafin Web client
share/tesserafin/web-revision.json   provenance of that web payload
LICENSE
```

## Requirements

The application payload carries its own .NET runtime, so no system .NET is
needed. It does need a few ordinary system libraries:

* `libicu` (globalization is on; the server refuses to start without it)
* `fontconfig` and a font package such as DejaVu (image and subtitle rendering)
* `libssl` / `openssl-libs`
* `glibc` 2.28 or newer

## Running it

Pick your own directories. Nothing is created for you and nothing defaults to a
system path.

```sh
PREFIX="$PWD"
./bin/tesserafin \
    --configdir "$PREFIX/state/config" \
    --datadir   "$PREFIX/state/data" \
    --cachedir  "$PREFIX/state/cache" \
    --logdir    "$PREFIX/state/log" \
    --webdir    "$PREFIX/share/tesserafin/web" \
    --ffmpeg    "$PREFIX/lib/tesserafin/ffmpeg/ffmpeg"
```

The server listens on port 8096. `http://127.0.0.1:8096/` redirects to `/web/`
and serves the first-run wizard.

`--ffmpeg` is not optional in practice: the server validates the encoder at
startup and refuses to start without a usable one. Always point it at the
bundled binary rather than letting it search `$PATH`, so you get the encoder this
build was tested against instead of whatever your distribution ships.

Run it as an unprivileged user. Nothing here needs root.

## Provenance

| Input | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Server commit | `@VCS_REF@` |
| Tesserafin Web commit | `@WEB_VCS_REF@` |
| jellyfin-ffmpeg | `@FFMPEG_VERSION@` (portable GPL build) |

`share/tesserafin/web-revision.json` records the web payload's own provenance as
the web build produced it.
